<title>CANADA: Canada to invest in Rhone-Poulenc unit.</title>
<headline>Canada to invest in Rhone-Poulenc unit.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada intends to invest in a unit of the French company Rhone-Poulenc SA for work on a cancer vaccine, the office of Prime Minister Jean Chretien said on Monday.</p>
<p>The investment in the subsidiary, Pasteur Merieux Connaught Canada, will be made under the federal government's Technology Partnership program.</p>
<p>The often criticized program provides interest-free money to companies on the understanding it will be paid back when a project becomes profitable.</p>
<p>Chretien will participate in the announcement in the company's laboratory in Toronto on Wednesday. Further details were not given.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
